34,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"The data reveals a significant disparity in reporting transparency. Software-based holdings rely solely on self-reported figures, while hardware-based ones allow for independent verification, though they introduce substantial delays and costs during audits.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"It is interesting to note the difference in verification. On my end, I've found that while our support recruitment is efficient, specialized field leadership takes much longer to secure, and our software partners are already quite stretched.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"It is quite telling, isn't it? I found that while some of our holdings are very steady with their customers, others struggled when prices rose. It makes me wonder about the true strength of their bonds.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"The financial flexibility is tighter than expected. Our reserve accounts are being depleted by follow-on calls at twice the modeled rate, and our credit line offers very little security against subscription-based assets.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shion,,"The pattern is clear. Our delays aren't internal; they're external. Security reviews for sensitive data take three times longer than others. If we pick a company in a regulated sector, expect a long wait before any revenue.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Misaki, @Shion, your findings suggest we are facing both financial strain and operational delays. If we add a company that requires external appraisals or long security reviews, our quarter-end reporting will only become more chaotic.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Misaki"",""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"I agree. We must consider the human cost as well. If we select a company requiring specialized field leadership or more software oversight, we may find ourselves unable to provide the necessary support.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"It is a bit worrying to hear about the strain you all are feeling. Perhaps we should look for a candidate that has a very loyal customer base and a simple, reliable delivery process.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Shizue, I agree. Given the rapid depletion of our reserves and the limitations of our credit line, we cannot afford a high-maintenance investment. We need a candidate with low capital intensity and predictable cash flows.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shion,,"Predictability is a luxury we can't afford to guess at. If we want to avoid the usual delays, we should prioritize a candidate whose product doesn't trigger these exhaustive security reviews. Simplicity is the only real hedge.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"It seems we are all converging on the need for simplicity. To protect our reporting cycle and financial health, we must avoid any candidate that adds audit complexity or requires heavy external verification.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"Indeed. A candidate that can operate independently, without demanding excessive time from our already overextended partners or relying on slow recruitment cycles, would be the most sustainable choice for us all.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"It is so heartening to see us all looking out for one another's well-being. Let us find a company that brings peace of mind and steady growth, rather than more stress to our lovely team.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Misaki,,Exactly. We need to be realistic about our current liquidity. A candidate that requires frequent follow-on capital or relies on assets we cannot borrow against would be a liability we cannot sustain right now.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shion,,"Let's stop pretending this is about ""well-being."" It's about risk. We need a lean operation that bypasses regulatory bottlenecks. If the candidate's deployment is stalled by a third party, the investment is a failure.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"We are in agreement on the criteria. We need a lean, low-maintenance candidate that avoids audit delays and regulatory bottlenecks. Let's see which of the candidates fits this profile of simplicity and transparency.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,I believe we have a clear set of constraints. Let us hope the candidates provide a path that allows us to maintain our balance and avoid further overextending our resources.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Shizue,,I agree. Let us hope we find a candidate that is not only successful but also kind to our resources and our spirits. I am ready to see who they are.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Misaki,,I agree. Let's move to the candidates. I'll be looking for the one that puts the least amount of pressure on our remaining liquidity and requires the fewest follow-on commitments.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shion,,I'm ready. Let's see which of these companies actually understands how to get a product into a customer's hands without getting bogged down in a nine-month security review.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over.""}]}"
